1
00:00:02,570 --> 00:00:12,400
Molly, I need your special talent for handling special matters.

2
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:15,800
Like what special matters?

3
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,300
Well, I have a scheduling problem.

4
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:18,946
Yes?

5
00:00:18,946 --> 00:00:21,900
I have three tonsillectomies set for Friday with Dr. Earl.

6
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:23,400
Yes?

7
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:26,800
I need to fit a fourth operation into his schedule.

8
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:30,676
And ... I know you can do it.

9
00:00:30,676 --> 00:00:31,700
Who's the patient?

10
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,600
Carl Herrera.

11
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,100
The boy has infected tonsils,

12
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:37,200
and we should remove them as soon as possible.

13
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,232
Well, I'll try to arrange the schedule, Dr. Stewart.

14
00:00:39,232 --> 00:00:42,600
But it's not going to be easy.

15
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:47,600
I know you'll be able to take care of it.

16
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:48,800
Well, Mrs. Herrera,

17
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,795
Carl will be perfectly fine after we remove his tonsils.

18
00:00:52,795 --> 00:00:55,304
Thank you for your reassurance, Dr. Stewart.

19
00:00:55,304 --> 00:00:58,000
He's had so many colds and sore throats recently.

20
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,645
Well, it's a very easy operation, Carl.

21
00:01:00,645 --> 00:01:02,056
You won't feel a thing.

22
00:01:02,056 --> 00:01:04,400
But when do they do it?

23
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,600
This Friday.

24
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:09,400
But Saturday's my birthday.

25
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:13,787
Well, we could reschedule the operation, Mrs. Herrera,

26
00:01:13,787 --> 00:01:16,100
but I don't want to put it off too long.

27
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:19,300
No, I think it's important to do it now.

28
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,000
We can have a birthday party for you, Carl,

29
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,300
When you come out of the hospital.

30
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:25,100
But it won't be on my birthday.

31
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:28,000
But your health is more important, Carl. Believe me.

32
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,800
I don't want my tonsils out.

33
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:40,500
Nurse Baker, would you come in, please?

34
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:46,200
Hello, Mrs. Herrera. Hi, Carl, how you doing?

35
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:49,508
I don't want my tonsils out.

36
00:01:49,508 --> 00:01:50,600
Come with me, Carl.

37
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:57,700
You and I will talk this over.

38
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,660
She has a special way with kids.

39
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:03,700
She sure does.

40
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:06,432
Carl, does your throat hurt?

41
00:02:06,432 --> 00:02:07,400
Yes.

42
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:10,117
OK. Do you want to get better?

43
00:02:10,117 --> 00:02:10,891
Yes.

44
00:02:10,891 --> 00:02:13,645
OK. We want you to get better, too.

45
00:02:13,645 --> 00:02:15,840
You'll have your tonsils out tomorrow,

46
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,908
and you won't get so many colds anymore.

47
00:02:17,908 --> 00:02:20,500
But if I have my tonsils out tomorrow,

48
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:23,300
I'll miss my birthday party on Saturday.

49
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:24,900
I know.

50
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:27,500
It's a problem, isn't it?

51
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:30,400
Let me try to work something out.

52
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,600
What?

53
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,700
I have to think about it.

54
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:35,100
You're fooling me.

55
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:37,000
Oh, I'm not, Carl.

56
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,400
Give me a chance to think about it,

57
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:41,448
and I'll come up with something.

58
00:02:41,448 --> 00:02:42,722
A surprise?

59
00:02:42,722 --> 00:02:43,300
Maybe.

60
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:45,436
But you just put on your pajamas and robe,

61
00:02:45,436 --> 00:02:48,300
and I'll think of a surprise.

62
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:49,800
Will it hurt?

63
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:50,200
No.

64
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,300
There are other boys and girls here,

65
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:52,400
and they're having their tonsils out.

66
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,884
You'll meet them.

67
00:02:53,884 --> 00:02:56,843
I don't want to.

68
00:02:56,843 --> 00:02:58,100
Change your clothes, Carl.

69
00:02:58,100 --> 00:03:01,100
Everything will be just fine.
